# ROM-derived assets.
#
# Everything under generated/ is extracted from the user's own legally-obtained
# ROM at build time and MUST NOT be committed -- the repo ships extractors and
# code, never the assets themselves.  Same model as Ship of Harkinian and the
# other static recomps.  Regenerate with:
#     pwsh tools/py.ps1 tools/assetpack/build_pak.py --rom <path-to-rom>
#
# NOT everything ROM-SHAPED belongs here.  src/data/gbc_palettes.c is committed
# on purpose: it is colour, not artwork, and nothing generates it.
generated/

# Build artifacts
build/
# the RED_ONLY tree (cmake -DRED_ONLY=ON), see README.md
build-red/
# and the same for a Blue-side tree -- a build dir is a build dir
build-blue/
# CI compile-check dir, and the local dir used to reproduce a
# fixture-headers build (tools/ci/gen_audio_id_fixture.py).
build-ci/
build-fixture/
# Any other build tree. Named dirs kept missing new ones: a Release tree for
# packaging Windows landed in a commit before this line existed.
build-*/
*.exe
*.dll
*.o
*.a
build_err*.txt
build_err.bin
build_out*.txt
gcc*.err
gcc*.out
tmp_gcc_*.txt

# Save files
*.sav

# Debug outputs
debug/screenshots/
debug.png
debug/dsl_bank_scene_npc.cfg
debug/dsl_bank_scene_npc.dat

# Per-slot vmap runtime cache (amberscript_mapbank.c's pks_mb_copy_file):
# every time a real map streams into one of the 8 rotating vmap slots
# (248-255), the engine copies that map's name-keyed placement file
# (mod_runtime/map_edits/vmap_<Name>.txt, real tracked content) into a
# slot-keyed mirror here so the slot machinery can address "whatever's
# currently in slot N" uniformly. Its content is just "whichever map was
# last visited in that slot this session" -- not an authored decision, and
# it gets silently rewritten by the game itself on every play session that
# touches those slots. Tracking it just produces phantom diffs unrelated
# to any real change (confirmed 2026-08-06: looked like a decoder/emitter
# regression, was actually two different play sessions visiting different
# maps in the same slot).
mod_runtime/map_edits/map_248.txt
mod_runtime/map_edits/map_249.txt
mod_runtime/map_edits/map_250.txt
mod_runtime/map_edits/map_251.txt
mod_runtime/map_edits/map_252.txt
mod_runtime/map_edits/map_253.txt
mod_runtime/map_edits/map_254.txt
mod_runtime/map_edits/map_255.txt
bird_*.png
.tmp_bird_contact.bmp
fly_*.log
make_fly.log
# The game's own runtime log. It was TRACKED, so every launch left the tree
# dirty and blocked anything that insists on a clean tree -- the release export
# among them. It is output, not source.
pokered_log.txt
oldamber_log.txt

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Reference disassemblies: clone these here manually (see README).  They carry
# their own ROM-derived assets, which is exactly what this repo must not, so
# they are never part of it -- they are read as source-of-truth ASM, as symbol
# tables for the extractors, and as verification oracles.
#
# One exception: pokered.sym. The extractors need it to build the asset pack, so
# without it a clone plus a ROM cannot build, and cloning a disassembly is not
# something this project asks anyone to do. It is `bank:addr Name` lines and
# carries no ROM bytes, and the release already ships it frozen inside setup
# (tools/dist/make_release.sh, --add-data). Tracking it changes where it comes
# from, not whether it is distributed.
#
# Written as a glob plus a negation because git does not descend into an
# excluded DIRECTORY, so `pokered-master/` with a negation after it would not
# work.
pokered-master/*
!pokered-master/pokered.sym
pokered-gbc-master/
pokecrystal-master/
redstarbluestar-master/
pokeyellow-master/

# Debug/export scratch and legacy ROM-derived art.  DIRECTORY rules, never
# per-file: this file's own history records that per-file entries are what let
# an archive walk out from under its rules during a rename and silently
# re-enter tracking.
#
# map_export/ is intermediate capture output -- kanto_map_export_offline.py
# regenerates it and is safe to re-run (docs/amberscript/import-pipeline.md).
# crystalsprites/ is superseded by tools/extract_crystal_mon_pics.py, which is
# ROM-only by construction and covers a strict superset.
#
# Untracked via `git rm -r --cached` 2026-08-04 (release-asset-pipeline-plan.md
# Phase 1b/2). Files remain on disk; only removed from git's index.
mods/gfx/crystalsprites/
mod_runtime/map_export/
mod_runtime/generated/
experiment/
maps/
debug/block.png
debug/cherrygrovebug.PNG
iconred.png
iconblue.png

# reference/hand_authored_kanto/ -- the 222 retired hand-authored Kanto maps
# (see its own README.md). Never loaded at runtime; kept ON DISK for local
# diffing against a freshly-generated map, but not tracked -- it is old,
# superseded content, not source.
reference/hand_authored_kanto/

# mnemo memory tree (project-local, regenerates from codebase)
.mnemo/
plugins/mnemo/

# Empty scratch file
powershell

# IDE / OS
.vscode/
*.user
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Packed archives (mnemo snapshots, source zips)
*.zip

# Debug suite lab workdirs (headless replay instances) and their loose
# screenshot/scratch output at repo root
lab_*/
lab_*.bmp

# Ad-hoc trace scratch dumps (debug-session byproduct, not source)
scratch_traces/

# debugsuite: generated battle cases (regenerate with tools/debugsuite/bgen.py)
tools/debugsuite/cases/matrix/
tools/debugsuite/cases/fuzz/
tools/debugsuite/cases/branches/

# The runtime asset pack: pure ROM data, built by the user from their own ROM
# via tools/assetpack/build_pak.py. Never committed, for the same reason
# generated/ is not.
assets.pak
*.pak

# Per-game packages and their manifests. One <id>.pak + <id>.json per source
# ROM, plus packages.txt giving the mount order -- all regenerated by
# build_pak.py, so the manifests are as derived as the archives they vouch for.
packages/

# ---- Kanto tile art: ROM-derived, 16,674 files ----
# <maplower>_tNNN.bin is RAW 2bpp lifted straight from the ROM's tileset
# graphics, and the .png beside it is the editable source that converts to it.
# The "custom_art" name is misleading -- none of this is hand-drawn. Measured:
# all 8331 .bin regenerate BYTE-IDENTICALLY from the ROM, and all 8331 .png
# regenerate PIXEL-IDENTICALLY (the committed ones are 2-bit greyscale, ours
# 8-bit -- irrelevant, since the game reads the .bin and only reconverts the
# .png when it is newer).
#
# Regenerate with:  pwsh tools/py.ps1 tools/romimport/emit_kanto.py --art-all
#
# DIRECTORY rule, not per-file: per-file entries are exactly what let the Johto
# archive walk out from under its own ignore rules during a rename and silently
# re-enter tracking.
mod_runtime/custom_art/kanto/

# ---- ROM-derived Johto import (proof of concept) ----
# Extracted from a Crystal ROM by the old disassembly-sourced importer
# (tools/pokecrystal_import.py).  ROM-derived assets are not committed --
# same rule as generated/.  Kept on disk, just not tracked; this Johto set
# was a proof of concept and is being replaced by tools/romimport/.
#
# The whole set now lives under _archive/johto_disasm/ (moved there by the
# Johto import branch).  That rename walked the files out from under the
# path-specific rules below and they became TRACKED again -- 1344 of them,
# while the archive's own README claimed they were not.  A directory rule is
# safe HERE, unlike below: this path holds nothing but the disassembly set.
mod_runtime/_archive/johto_disasm/
